WEBVTT

q0001
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.354
Can an experiment reproduce perfectly and still fail its reason for deployment?

q0002
00:00:06.354 --> 00:00:15.563
This episode has one job: D8 reproduced exact outputs and rule incidence on Linux but reversed the Windows profitability direction, so unconditional one-pass rewriting was not promoted.

q0003
00:00:15.563 --> 00:00:24.772
We build on Milestones D-D7: task routing, proved rules, caching, and normalization; their definitions stay fixed while this lesson adds a new layer.

q0004
00:00:24.772 --> 00:00:33.091
D8 froze the one-pass rewrite package and checked exactness, rule incidence, and whole-task profitability on Linux.

q0005
00:00:33.091 --> 00:00:40.918
Watch for the label frozen confirmation; it stays attached to the artifact this episode means.

q0006
00:00:40.918 --> 00:00:48.254
When we say rule incidence, the highlight identifies its layer before we interpret it.

q0007
00:00:48.254 --> 00:00:57.064
The term profitability transfer receives its own visual state so it cannot drift into a neighboring concept.

q0008
00:00:57.064 --> 00:01:03.418
We will keep negative control visible whenever its definition controls the inference.

q0009
00:01:03.418 --> 00:01:12.228
The next sequence uses Versioned policy rules as a conceptual teaching example, not as measured benchmark evidence.

q0010
00:01:12.228 --> 00:01:16.126
Our stable example is Versioned policy rules.

q0011
00:01:16.126 --> 00:01:23.953
A conceptual access policy over role, region, resource, and risk, shown across three source revisions.

q0012
00:01:23.953 --> 00:01:29.816
Teach related rules, exact reuse, changed-region invalidation, and charged rewrite overhead.

q0013
00:01:29.816 --> 00:01:37.152
We now construct the Versioned policy rules and name every part before interpreting it.

q0014
00:01:37.152 --> 00:01:46.361
Freeze the Windows package, carry identical rules and inputs to Linux, and verify exact outputs and application counts first.

q0015
00:01:46.361 --> 00:01:52.224
Reveal the reversed overhead-inclusive timing only after correctness and incidence match.

q0016
00:01:52.224 --> 00:01:57.596
Now isolate exactness versus profitability separation inside Versioned policy rules.

q0017
00:01:57.596 --> 00:02:06.805
The example definition and output meaning stay fixed while only the state for exactness versus profitability separation changes.

q0018
00:02:06.805 --> 00:02:16.014
That matched before-and-after view assigns the visible consequence to exactness versus profitability separation, not to a substituted workload.

q0019
00:02:16.014 --> 00:02:20.895
Exactness and rule-incidence checks turn green in both lanes.

q0020
00:02:20.895 --> 00:02:30.104
The frozen one-pass rewrite result changed from 1.050x on Windows to 0.929x on Linux, so unconditional one-pass rewriting was not promoted.

q0021
00:02:30.104 --> 00:02:36.458
Read that statement only within this scope: Milestone D8 frozen Linux confirmation.

q0022
00:02:36.458 --> 00:02:40.847
Its declared measurement boundary is overhead-inclusive one-pass rewrite.

q0023
00:02:40.847 --> 00:02:45.236
The uncertainty field says one bounded cross-machine confirmation.

q0024
00:02:45.236 --> 00:02:54.445
The nearest confusing lesson is D9 abstention policy: safe, charged, not promoted; it owns D9 calibrated policy, while this episode owns D8 frozen Linux transfer.

q0025
00:02:54.445 --> 00:03:02.272
Named rule nodes combine those inputs into one exact allow-or-deny result under a declared ordering.

q0026
00:03:02.272 --> 00:03:08.626
Holding that element fixed lets this episode isolate exactness versus profitability separation.

q0027
00:03:08.626 --> 00:03:14.980
A changed-region trace distinguishes reusable structure from rules that must be recomputed.

q0028
00:03:14.980 --> 00:03:22.807
Detection, rewrite, persistence, and extraction costs remain visible instead of disappearing into a reuse label.

q0029
00:03:22.807 --> 00:03:31.617
The example teaches a revision workload and does not claim measured behavior for a deployed policy engine.

q0030
00:03:31.617 --> 00:03:39.444
The final decision check compares exact outputs before any preparation or wrapper ratio is interpreted.

q0031
00:03:39.444 --> 00:03:47.271
Exact transfer passed, but profitability did not; the negative result is the final promotion authority.

q0032
00:03:47.271 --> 00:03:54.607
Choose the correct promotion decision when exactness and incidence pass but overhead-inclusive speed loses.

q0033
00:03:54.607 --> 00:04:01.943
D8 is an exact engineering success and a profitability failure at the same time.

q0034
00:04:01.943 --> 00:04:07.315
Now isolate D8 frozen Linux transfer inside Versioned policy rules.

q0035
00:04:07.315 --> 00:04:16.524
The example definition and output meaning stay fixed while only the state for D8 frozen Linux transfer changes.

q0036
00:04:16.524 --> 00:04:25.733
That matched before-and-after view assigns the visible consequence to D8 frozen Linux transfer, not to a substituted workload.

q0037
00:04:25.733 --> 00:04:32.087
Windows and Linux lanes share frozen package, input, rule, and digest identities.

q0038
00:04:32.087 --> 00:04:39.423
Role, region, resource, and risk remain the stable inputs to the conceptual access decision.

q0039
00:04:39.423 --> 00:04:45.777
Holding that element fixed lets this episode isolate D8 frozen Linux transfer.

q0040
00:04:45.777 --> 00:04:52.622
Three adjacent revisions change bounded rule regions while unchanged nodes retain their identities.

q0041
00:04:52.622 --> 00:05:00.941
Reuse is valid only when source identity, revision identity, and the output contract all still match.

q0042
00:05:00.941 --> 00:05:08.768
A safe fallback evaluates the full exact policy whenever the incremental contract cannot be proved.

q0043
00:05:08.768 --> 00:05:17.578
Repeated queries and adjacent revisions are separate reuse axes, so their break-even points must be measured separately.

q0044
00:05:17.578 --> 00:05:26.787
The starting state preserves the stable definition: A conceptual access policy over role, region, resource, and risk, shown across three source revisions.

q0045
00:05:26.787 --> 00:05:35.996
A common mistake is this: Reproducing exact outputs and rule counts is sufficient to promote a performance optimization.

q0046
00:05:35.996 --> 00:05:42.350
Repair it by returning to the owned distinction: D8 frozen Linux transfer.

q0048
00:05:45.420 --> 00:05:54.629
Use the episode's central distinction to answer: D8 is an exact engineering success and a profitability failure at the same time.

q0049
00:05:54.629 --> 00:06:00.001
Reproduction includes the failed criterion, not only the successful checks.
